## Development

```bash
npm install
cp .env.example .env.local   # point OBSIDIAN_VAULT at a test vault
npm run dev                  # watch build + deploy into the vault (hot reload)
```

Install the community **Hot Reload** plugin in the test vault once — dev builds
write a `.hotreload` marker so every rebuild reloads the plugin in place.

## Quality gates

```bash
npm run lint && npm run check:loc && npm run check:css && npm run check:quality
npm run typecheck && npm run test
npm run build && npm run check:artifacts
```

See `docs/quality-integration-guide.md` for how the ratchets work.

## Release

```bash
npm version patch   # bumps package.json + manifest.json + versions.json
git push --follow-tags
```

The tag push builds and attaches `main.js`, `manifest.json`, and `styles.css`
to a GitHub release (when the release workflow is enabled).
